    "body": "The competing-record reader needed an all-bank training instrument, but its original question registry mixed current residence with unsupported origin/address questions. This adds Rust plan/panel construction and an explicit supported-current-role policy: statements establish current job/residence, questions ask only those facts, and donor literals, chronology and update/reassertion acts remain bound. Derived provenance identifies newly authored wording. Legacy data and prior synthetic pilots are retained.\n\nBoth current records and their assertion cues remain available to the learned geometric reader. No supplied selected answer, query-role label or gold filter enters runtime. The numerical reader/root learner is unchanged. A public context-horizon guard prevents invalid final reads. Exact template/store controls establish protocol reachability; they do not establish learned attention or English generalization.\n\nActual execution at83d6722f:49 release tests (plan5/panel18/observation26), release of three examples, corrected construction128/32 and zero-update native admission128rows/1268positions pass. Hard-forward parity and frozen-input invariants pass; root gradients finite, norm0.00323017046; CE1.138694423. Unchanged parent completes10/128. No corrected-data fit/evaluation predictions. Independent saved-data audit passes5332 checks. Every donor history is reused and all12 query strings occur in both splits: the32-row evaluation is diagnostic rewritten-packet coverage, not unexposed semantic/payload/history/query transfer. Freeze untouched transfer inputs before claiming transfer.\n\nTwo old-panel order fits and one deliberately interrupted30-update run are preserved; no three-order/chat verdict. Exact delivery9291b563 source/docs review passes; final-head scoped Rust checks PASS (49 tests and three release builds) and receipts are posted on the PR. Formatting, whitespace and claim-wording checks pass. No GPU/Metal or laptop performance claim. Shared session/compiler seam unchanged.\n\nReferences #820, #1552. No issue closure or model promotion.\n",
